nodecode-disciplined-vibe-coding is a rewrite of bmtrnavsky's bmtrnavsky/disciplined-vibe-coding:

  https://github.com/bmtrnavsky/disciplined-vibe-coding
  commit ac4de52dc8baf9ece90e3a2bab749152ae93a91b
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Brad Trnavsky (LICENSE)

The original is a plugin whose one code path registers eleven SKILL.md files.
Rewritten here: each of those eleven files is one prose define-skill, its
frontmatter description the sentence the index lists, its remaining
frontmatter and its whole body kept as comment lines, so (help 'name) reads
the procedure as the author wrote it and nothing is evaluated. The markdown the
skills name -- the economy ladder and the to-spec, writing-plan and wayfinder
templates -- is carried unchanged in guides/ and is read from there.

Left out: the plugin's opt-in shell hook, which reminded the model once a turn
that no docs had been logged in 40 minutes, and its update script, which
replaced the plugin's own files from a source tree. A knowledge cell runs
nothing, and Nodecode installs a cell at a pinned commit, so neither has a job
here. Also left out, because the skills never name them: the plugin's own
README, CATALOG, HOOKS and UPDATE pages, its user templates, and its
self-check script.

LICENSE is the original's, unchanged, and its closing paragraph names that
repository's ATTRIBUTIONS.md and SOURCE-LICENSES.md, which this cell does not
carry: the lineage of each skill rides its own "Lineage:" line in the skill's
text.
